      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should these two lines be reversed to guarantee no overflow? `-\u003d old_size` should always be legal, because `old_size` is currently in the `lru_count`. Since `new_size` is supposed to be smaller than `old_size`, it should be legal to `+\u003d new_size` afterwards.\n\nHowever, if you imagine a case where a range was 2.1 GB in size and was decreased to 2.05 GB in size, `+\u003d new_size` would technically overflow. This won\u0027t cause a bug in practice, because Rust unsigned overflow is defined, but if sanitizers are turned on it could trip.",
      "revId": "1125f0114a26ac6893a3fc1ae369d59cc14c7045",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
